Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: context variable is accessible in functions")
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-ImplCont-001
val logger = TestLogger(messages: 0, last_msg: "")
__ctx_logger = logger
_lex("x = 1")
expect(__ctx_logger.count()).to_be_greater_than(0)
```

</details>

#### functions share the same context variable

- Verify: functions share the same context variable
   - Expected: __ctx_logger.count() equals `3)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 7 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: functions share the same context variable")
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-ImplCont-001
val logger = TestLogger(messages: 0, last_msg: "")
__ctx_logger = logger
_compile("x = 1")
# _compile calls _parse which calls _lex - all 3 log calls go to same logger
expect(__ctx_logger.count()).to_equal(3)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
```

</details>

#### last logged message is from deepest function call

- Verify: last logged message is from deepest function call


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 7 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: last logged message is from deepest function call")
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-ImplCont-001
val logger = TestLogger(messages: 0, last_msg: "")
__ctx_logger = logger
_compile("hello")
# _lex is called last, logs "lexing: hello"
expect(__ctx_logger.last()).to_start_with("lexing:")
```

</details>

#### context variable can be swapped for different loggers

- Verify: context variable can be swapped for different loggers
   - Expected: count1 equals `1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract`
   - Expected: count2 equals `1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 15 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: context variable can be swapped for different loggers")
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-ImplCont-001
val logger1 = TestLogger(messages: 0, last_msg: "first")
val logger2 = TestLogger(messages: 0, last_msg: "second")

__ctx_logger = logger1
_lex("a")
val count1 = __ctx_logger.count()

__ctx_logger = logger2
_lex("b")
val count2 = __ctx_logger.count()

expect(count1).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
expect(count2).to_equal(1)  # oracle: value fixed by the spec contract
```

</details>

#### save-set-restore pattern preserves outer context

- Verify: save-set-restore pattern preserves outer context
   - Expected: __ctx_logger.count() equals `1)  # outer logger only saw "y"`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 17 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: save-set-restore pattern preserves outer context")
# @req: REQ-FEATURE-ImplCont-001
val outer_logger = TestLogger(messages: 0, last_msg: "outer")
val inner_logger = TestLogger(messages: 0, last_msg: "inner")

__ctx_logger = outer_logger

# Simulate: with_context(logger: inner_logger): _lex("x")
val __saved_logger_0 = __ctx_logger
__ctx_logger = inner_logger
_lex("x")
__ctx_logger = __saved_logger_0

# After restore, outer logger is active again
_lex("y")
expect(__ctx_logger.last()).to_start_with("lexing: y")
expect(__ctx_logger.count()).to_equal(1)  # outer logger only saw "y"
```

</details>

